WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.976
A floor robot drives on a
grid of squares on the floor.

2
00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:11.911
Press its buttons, press GO,
and off it goes to the shop.

3
00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:15.987
This is a floor robot. It
drives on a grid of squares.

4
00:00:16.207 --> 00:00:20.804
On its back are buttons: forward,
backwards, turn left, turn right.

5
00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:25.204
The shop is three squares ahead,
so press forward three times.

6
00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:29.650
Every press is remembered, in
order. That list is the program.

7
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.725
Press GO, and it runs them
all, one square at a time.

8
00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:37.568
The robot keeps every press
you make until you clear it.

9
00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:41.271
Press CLEAR first. That
wipes the old program away.

10
00:00:41.491 --> 00:00:45.206
Forget CLEAR, and your new
presses join on to the old ones.

11
00:00:45.426 --> 00:00:49.142
The robot sets off doing both,
and stops in the wrong place.

12
00:00:49.362 --> 00:00:53.681
It is not confused. So clear
it, enter the presses, then GO.

13
00:00:54.181 --> 00:00:58.035
Each press of the forward button
moves the robot one square.

14
00:00:58.255 --> 00:01:02.110
Each turn spins it a quarter
turn. It does not move at all.

15
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:05.813
Count the squares. The house is
two up, then two to the right.

16
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:09.655
Forward, forward, turn right,
forward, forward: five presses.

17
00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:13.404
Press GO, and the robot drives
all the way to the house.

18
00:01:13.904 --> 00:01:18.316
Every journey has a destination:
the shop, home, school.

19
00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:21.926
This time a wall is in the way.
You cannot drive through it.

20
00:01:22.146 --> 00:01:25.304
Turn before you reach it, and
go round it to the school.

21
00:01:25.524 --> 00:01:30.818
Forward, turn left, forward.
Turn right, forward, forward.

22
00:01:31.038 --> 00:01:34.336
Turn right, then forward,
and the robot is at school.

23
00:01:34.836 --> 00:01:38.179
Before you press GO, follow
the program in your head.

24
00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:41.789
Move your finger one square
for every forward press.

25
00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:46.235
This robot faces down. Forward,
forward: two squares down.

26
00:01:46.455 --> 00:01:50.310
Turn left. It faces right
now, but it has not moved.

27
00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.641
One more forward, and your
finger is on the shop.

28
00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:57.391
Now press GO, and the robot
stops on the shop too.

29
00:01:57.891 --> 00:02:01.327
Big robots follow the same
kind of program as yours.

30
00:02:01.547 --> 00:02:05.355
A warehouse robot drives to
shelf fourteen, then stops.

31
00:02:05.575 --> 00:02:09.105
A hospital robot turns left
at the right ward door.

32
00:02:09.325 --> 00:02:14.805
A robot vacuum turns when it bumps.
A delivery robot finds house numbers.

33
00:02:15.305 --> 00:02:17.998
The buttons on its back
make up the program.

34
00:02:18.218 --> 00:02:20.958
CLEAR first, then all
the presses, then GO.

35
00:02:21.178 --> 00:02:24.290
One press is one square.
A turn only spins.

36
00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.807
Predict where it will stop,
then press GO and see.
